  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Hellenic Mining Company is a Cypriot mining and industrial business. It joined Australian company Oxiana in establishing Hellenic Copper Mines in 1994 to develop the island’s remaining low grade copper reserves. That venture restarted production at Skouriotissa, using leaching and electrochemical processing to produce copper cathodes for export to European markets.",
    "html": "<p>Hellenic Mining Company is a Cypriot mining and industrial business. It joined Australian company Oxiana in establishing Hellenic Copper Mines in 1994 to develop the island’s remaining low grade copper reserves. That venture restarted production at Skouriotissa, using leaching and electrochemical processing to produce copper cathodes for export to European markets.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 51,
    "confidence": {
      "score": 94,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Public corporate sources support the institutional activities and historical chronology; no present shareholding or operating scale is inferred."
    },
