  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Hellenic Mining Company developed exploration partnerships alongside its mining interests. In 1998 it and Oxiana established an equal joint venture to investigate base and precious metals across Cyprus. The venture operated through Eastern Mediterranean Minerals, with Oxiana supplying senior management and Hellenic Mining Company contributing access to mining and exploration tenements. The agreement excluded the immediate area around the existing Hellenic Copper Mines operation.\n\nThe partners began drilling the Redhills gold prospect south of Nicosia. Their programme examined mineralisation beneath earlier workings and combined drilling with mapping and sampling. Wider plans included geochemical sampling and airborne surveys along the northern and eastern flanks of the Troodos Mountains.",
